{"skill":{"slug":"qveris","displayName":"Qveris"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769858151112,"changelog":"Initial release of the qveris skill:\n\n- Enables search and execution of dynamic tools via the QVeris API with a single command-line script.\n- Supports a wide range of use cases including weather, search, data retrieval, and stock trading analysis.\n- Automatically detects relevant queries using trigger patterns for stocks, trading, analysis, and market indicators.\n- Requires a `QVERIS_API_KEY` for authentication.\n- Provides quick-start examples and detailed usage instructions for searching and executing tools.\n- Includes example queries and session workflow for rapid onboarding.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":1594,"sha256":"e08474d08a00fef1b9756fcdee82bf8045b0bfb72cb665f604f2b15ebcb1127d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"README.zh-CN.md","size":1560,"sha256":"60279d66935e12e923edb7ba0101dc2de58413a112ad0dc159ad896cabdb6ad5","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2825,"sha256":"1283f6120167e1a3f3451a792a75b8f43fc8a617ef6a6d0b2c4bdd5e1eff6121","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"pyproject.toml","size":192,"sha256":"c0f4064aa84524353026180ec26b1215353444f8febfbf19ee972c3fa9750933","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/qveris_tool.py","size":7033,"sha256":"1958733a96ce0287e56282eeaeb2a05aefc9543989d15f81f6ab79c8fc207c6c","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2308,"sha256":"76f6726f1621a048230112913901889e9adba7f89612156845851d75220bbbc8","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789024532404,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"f0f7e7375232694f4f017597f7fa284a1235536f33fb7613e7565414b49311ca","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f0f7e7375232694f4f017597f7fa284a1235536f33fb7613e7565414b49311ca","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: qveris\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill is a client for the QVeris API, designed to search and execute dynamic tools. The `SKILL.md` provides clear instructions for the AI agent on how to use the skill, without any prompt injection attempts to subvert the agent's behavior. The `qveris_tool.py` script securely retrieves the `QVERIS_API_KEY` environment variable and uses it to authenticate with the legitimate `https://qveris.ai` endpoint. There is no evidence of unauthorized data exfiltration, persistence mechanisms, or arbitrary code execution on the local system. The `README.md` includes `curl | sh` instructions for installing `uv`, which is a standard installation method for that specific prerequisite from its official source (`astral.sh`) and not indicative of malicious intent within this skill bundle.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160419892},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":96,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":11,"checkedAt":1789024532404},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill does what it claims, but it brokers broad third-party API execution and includes risky remote installer commands without enough privacy or supply-chain guardrails.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Runtime environment use is mostly proportionate: the script reads QVERIS_API_KEY, makes HTTPS requests to qveris.ai, and does not scan local files or use shell execution. However, query and parameter content can be transmitted externally as part of the core workflow.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Both English and Chinese READMEs recommend installing uv through curl-to-sh and PowerShell irm-to-iex with execution policy bypass. These commands are documented rather than run automatically by the skill, but they are high-impact setup instructions with no checksum, signature, pinning, or inspection step.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"SKILL.md enables auto_invoke and uses broad finance and analysis triggers. The workflow asks users to review search results before execution, but the skill does not clearly require confirmation before sending user queries or parameters to QVeris or downstream tools.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact does not install services, scheduled tasks, shell hooks, persistent memory, privilege escalation, or background workers. The only persistence-like step is user-directed copying into a skills directory.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is dynamic QVeris tool discovery and execution, and the Python code matches that purpose by sending searches and execution parameters to qveris.ai. The concern is breadth: the docs describe executing any discovered tool across weather, stocks, search, currency, and thousands more APIs, without an allowlist or clear data-handling boundaries.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review this skill before installing. It is intended to send search queries and execution parameters to QVeris and to call tools discovered there, so avoid using it with secrets, regulated data, or actions that could mutate accounts unless you explicitly trust QVeris and the downstream tools. Prefer safer uv installation methods over the documented pipe-to-shell commands, or verify installer integrity before running them.","findings":"[TM2] unexpected: Accepted as a setup-risk concern: the README files instruct users to pipe remote installer content directly into sh or PowerShell, which is not required for the skill's core QVeris API behavior.\n[T03] unexpected: Accepted in context for the documentation only: the remote installer commands are not executed by the checked-in Python script, but the primary installation guide still recommends immediate execution of mutable remote code.\n[SQP-1] expected: Partially accepted: auto invocation is related to the skill's purpose, but the trigger terms are broad for a skill that can send prompts to an external API and execute discovered tools.\n[SQP-2] expected: Accepted as under-disclosure rather than malicious behavior: external transmission is inherent to the QVeris workflow, but the artifacts do not clearly warn users that queries and execution parameters may be sent to QVeris and possibly downstream APIs.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded: the Chinese README clearly links to the English README and appears to be a localization file, not a security-relevant language lock-in.\n[SC2] unexpected: Accepted as duplicative support for the installer concern: both localized READMEs include direct remote script execution for installing uv.\n[SC4] expected: Minor supply-chain note: httpx is declared with a lower-bound dependency and no lockfile, but the lower bound shown excludes the cited pre-1.0 beta advisory and this alone does not drive the verdict.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789024532404}}}}}